{
  "$comment": "Frequency presets surfaced in the Bands panel. Each group renders as a collapsible section. `hz` is the desired listen frequency; `vfo_offset_hz` (optional, default 0) shifts the SDR centre off the signal to avoid a DC-spike pollution \u2014 applied as center_freq_hz = hz + vfo_offset_hz and freq_shift_hz = -vfo_offset_hz, so the signal still lands at baseband. `mode` drives the panel's two actions: the `Tune` button moves frequency only (demod chain unchanged), while `+RX` loads the canonical receiver preset for `mode` (WFM\u2192wbfm, NBFM\u2192nbfm, AM\u2192wbam, USB\u2192usb, LSB\u2192lsb, CW\u2192cw, FT8/FT4\u2192ft8-ft8/ft8-ft4, WSPR\u2192wspr, NAVTEX\u2192navtex, AIS\u2192ais, ADS-B\u2192adsb, ISM\u2192rtl433-433, WX\u2192nwr, APRS\u2192packet; remaining HF data modes are authored as USB pending the bandplan hard-ref pass) then tunes \u2014 a coherent end-to-end chain, same as picking it from the Signal Catalog. `+RX` is disabled when no receiver preset matches the mode (data-only GMSK/Pulse/OOK\u00b7FSK) or that preset isn't installed in this build. User-editable.",
